{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And he said, etc. — when you look upon, etc.</b> One must examine for what purpose this act of seeing is; he should have said only ״if it is a son״ etc., and all the more so according to the words of our Sages of blessed memory (Sotah 11b) who said that he gave them a sign — for a male, its face is downward; for a female, its face is upward — I do not know why these signs were necessary. Further, one must examine his reason for why he did not decree upon all of them; and one should not believe of him that he conducted himself with the attribute of mercy in order to leave them a remnant in the land, for his root is a root of cruelty. Further, it is difficult that he said <b>and you shall kill him</b> with the addition of the letter vav, without any prior action to introduce the matter. Further, why was it necessary to say <b>if it is a daughter, she shall live</b>, since Pharaoh decreed only upon the males — it is obvious that the midwives would not seek to uproot them all?" "<b>Indeed</b> this wicked man acted cunningly so that the plan would succeed in his hand, for who is the woman who would volunteer herself to serve as a midwife in order to kill her own children? Therefore he acted cunningly and said to them that they should conduct themselves in this manner and do it covertly, without the women in labor feeling anything along these lines — for before the newborn is known what it is, whether male or female, the midwives would look upon the birth-stool: if it is a male, they would kill him and say he was stillborn, and they would not wait until he emerges and cries out (cf. Sotah 12a); rather, they would look upon the birth-stool before he comes out into the world, whether he is male. And how would they know? Therefore our Sages of blessed memory said that he gave them a sign. And this is why it says <b>and you shall kill him</b> with the addition of the letter vav — for the first command he gave them was to distinguish and determine whether it is male before he comes out into the world and gives forth his voice, and the second is <b>and you shall kill him</b> upon his emergence from his mother's womb." "And his saying <b>if it is a daughter</b> etc. — he further intended by this that through the medium of this arrangement the laboring women would not sense anything of the matter, for when they see that sometimes their infants survive, they would not suspect the midwives, and they would not discern that they are killing the males and not the females. Or perhaps he commanded them not to announce the male but to say that the newborn was stillborn — for through this means the suspicion would be concealed. And with this all the fine points are resolved." "<b>And behold</b> a wise plan Pharaoh devised in this matter, so that they would not be able to rise up from the land — namely, that through the killing of every male and the multiplication of women, and since a woman prefers to marry (Aramaic: טַב לְמֵיתַב טַן דּוּ), the women of Israel would join with the Egyptians and intermarry with them, and from now on there would be no possibility of rising up from the land once they become one people. Moreover, the holy souls would be impaired through the mingling with impure souls, and they would remain there forever — Heaven forfend. And you will find that our Sages of blessed memory said (Leviticus Rabbah 32:5) that Israel was not redeemed until four things were present among them, one of them being that they guarded themselves from forbidden relations; and concerning this it is explicit in the Kabbalah (Song of Songs 4:12): ״A garden locked״ etc.; and had they intermarried with the Egyptians, Heaven forfend, there would have been no rising up against their enemies."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The word וְעַוֵּי in the Hebrew, marked by the editor with the parenthetical gloss צועק ('crying out') and a cross-reference to Sotah 12a, appears to be a variant or possibly corrupt form; I have translated it hyper-literally in context as 'cries out' per the parenthetical note."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:23:22.908875101Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}